'''Juan Ignacio Sánchez Brown''' (born May 8, 1977),<ref>{{Cite web |url=http://www.acb.com/jugador.php?id=B1E |title=ACB.com Pepe Sánchez nacionalidad{{!}}licencia: ESP |access-date=2005-12-05 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20060113025337/http://www.acb.com/jugador.php?id=B1E |archive-date=2006-01-13 |url-status=dead }}</ref> commonly known as '''Pepe Sánchez''', is an Argentine former professional [[basketball]] player. He played at the [[point guard]] position. He was a part of [[Argentina national basketball team|Argentina]]'s [[Basketball at the 2004 Summer Olympics – Men's tournament|2004 Olympic]] gold medal team and was the first Argentine to play in the [[National Basketball Association|NBA]]. He played two seasons in the NBA, playing in a total of 38 games with the [[Philadelphia 76ers]] (24 games), [[Atlanta Hawks]] (5 games), and the [[Detroit Pistons]] (9 games), averaging only 5 minutes per game.

